  <result aggregation-status="1" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSO deepen linkages with communities/groups</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSO deepen linkages with communities/groups</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSO deepen linkages with communities/groups</narrative>
    </title>
    <reference code="SCS074fr" indicator-uri="http://helpdesk-opendata-minbuza.nl/indicator-codelist" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline iso-date="2021-09-01" value="1" year="2021"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-09-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="23">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">We can demonstrate that 23 organisations created deeper linkages with communities and groups as a result of the CSF intervention in Year 1 and 2 of CSF2.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="23">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The CSF project emphasized the importance of deepened linkages between CSOs and the communities they serve, aiming for genuine representation and community-driven agendas. Remarkably, all supported CSOs demonstrated a strong connection with their local communities, ensuring that the issues they addressed were authentic and rooted in community needs. Unsurprisingly, the small beginners scored highly in this aspect during the exit OCA given their proximity to the grassroots. This success underscores the project&apos;s achievement in fostering meaningful collaboration between CSOs and the communities they represent, reinforcing the notion that impactful change must emerge organically from the grassroots. The commitment to community-driven initiatives has not only solidified the legitimacy of the supported CSOs but has also contributed to more effective and relevant interventions, showcasing the tangible benefits of aligning organizational efforts with local contexts.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSOs form alliances between themselves and with other actors to work on issues relevant to needs and priorities of the communities</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSO form alliances between themselves and with other actors to work on issues relevant to needs and priorities of the communities</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSOs form alliances between themselves and with other actors to work on issues relevant to needs and priorities of the communities</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSO form alliances between themselves and with other actors to work on issues relevant to needs and priorities of the communities. Under CSF2 we have a separate &#x2018;Networking&#x2019; window. Though this window will become operational during year 2 of CSF2, we have evidence from CSF1 that 1 alliance is operational in Yambio.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline iso-date="2021-09-01" value="1" year="2021">
     <location ref="South Sudan"></location>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-09-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="5"></target>
     <actual value="5">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Throughout the project, a powerful outcome has emerged as CSOs formed alliances among themselves and with other stakeholders to tackle complex issues aligned with community needs. This collaborative spirit emphasizes that in addressing multifaceted challenges, unity is paramount. In the prevailing restrictive environment, CSOs have recognized the vulnerability of a lone voice and the strength derived from building solidarity. While competition persists, primarily due to limited funding, the CSF project has successfully instilled an appreciation within CSOs for the value of forging alliances. This shift reflects a strategic understanding that collective efforts amplify impact and contribute to a more resilient and influential civil society.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSOs demonstrated increased capacity to influence and engage with decision makers</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSOs demonstrated increased capacity to influence and engage with decision makers</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of CSO which demonstrated increased capacity to influence and engage with decision makers</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of CSO which demonstrated increased capacity to influence and engage with decision makers, in creating space for CSO demands and positions through agenda setting, influencing the debate and/or creating space to engage at sub-national level</narrative>
    </description>
    <reference code="SCS032fr" indicator-uri="http://helpdesk-opendata-minbuza.nl/indicator-codelist" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline iso-date="2022-09-01" value="1" year="2021"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-09-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-08-31"></period-end>
     <target value="39">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project dedicated substantial efforts to bolstering the advocacy capacity of CSOs, recognizing its pivotal role in influencing and engaging decision makers. Although the landscape of advocacy remains challenging for many grantees, there emerged distinct pockets of success. These successes underscore the CSF&apos;s impact, demonstrating that despite the persistent challenges in the advocacy arena, the strategic investment in strengthening CSOs&apos; capacity has yielded tangible and noteworthy results. CSOs, equipped with enhanced advocacy skills, have made strides in effectively influencing decision makers, marking a positive outcome in the broader landscape of civic engagement.A pivotal success across the entire portfolio lies in the strengthened capacity of CSOs to engage constructively with decision makers, even within restrictive environments. This achievement is not confined to CSOs primarily focused on advocacy; instead, it resonated even with CSOs that are primarily focused on services. With training and support from CSF, these CSOs have been able to expand their &#x201C;narrow&#x201D; mission of service delivery to include advocacy as a means of furthering their service-delivery objective. CSOs, supported by our project, assumed leadership roles in advocacy on critical issues, extending beyond social issues to actively influence matters related to political and civic space.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="39"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased Lobby and Advocacy capacities</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased Lobby and Advocacy capacities</narrative>
